# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*

# Python virtual environment
.venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# temp workspaces
#
# The sandbox is scratch, WITH TWO EXCEPTIONS. Ruled 2026-08-03: the minimal
# case is a sandbox-only test bed whose entire output is (a) the emitted prompt
# and (b) the transcript. Those are the evidence for the part-context evolution
# design discussions, and evidence that only exists on disk cannot be diffed
# circle against circle, and dies to a `git clean`.
#
# `work/sandbox/*` rather than `work/sandbox/`, deliberately: git
# cannot re-include anything beneath an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a `!` line under
# the directory form would silently do nothing. Excluding the children instead
# leaves the directory itself readable, and the two negations below then apply.
# Moved from coordinator/sandbox/, R176, 2026-08-15 — coordinator/ is product
# domain and this is transcript-derived content.
# A MEMO, NOT A RECORD. work/token_counts.json holds sha256 -> token count
# for prompt prefixes the model service has already counted (R260,
# 2026-08-20). It makes no claim about this project — losing it costs one
# re-count and nothing else — and it would otherwise churn in every diff
# whenever a practice, a briefing or a distillate moved.
work/token_counts.json
work/sandbox/*
!work/sandbox/prompts/
!work/sandbox/circles/
work/nightly/

# Tool working databases — rewritten constantly, ~11MB each time
.fileintel/

# Run logs — derived, one per run (circle_audit.py, renamed from
# nightly.py 2026-08-19 — R228 removed the batch shape, this file
# retired from scripts/ into coordinator/ the same day)
work/logs/circle_audit*.log

# TWO MEMOS, NOT RECORDS — 2026-08-26. Both are written by a live circle,
# both were tracked by nothing, and so both sat dirty in the working tree
# forever after: enough, in the lab, to deadlock a `pull-main`, which
# refuses a dirty tree. Ignored rather than committed because each is
# superseded by something that IS the record, and neither loses anything
# by staying untracked — they are read off local disk, never out of git:
#   closing_<OT>.json  the START-OF-CLOSE marker. mark_close_started():
#                      "IT IS NEVER DELETED. A close report supersedes it",
#                      and close_<OT>.json beside it is committed.
#   dream_<OT>.json    phase 2's run marker. The `dream/<OT>` git tag is
#                      the evidence a circle was processed; the file is
#                      already_processed()'s second reader, kept for the
#                      tree where git cannot answer at all (R349), and
#                      still on disk there whether git tracks it or not.
# The registers a circle writes — self/working_sets.toml, self/proposals.toml
# — are the opposite case and are STAGED by the close now, not ignored.
#
# `dream_[0-9]*` AND NOT `dream_*`: dream_error_<OT>.json is a FAILURE REPORT,
# a real diagnostic naming what refused and how to re-run, and it stays
# visible on purpose. inter_circle.py globs the run marker the same way, for
# the same reason.
#   delta_<OT>.json    circle_delta's close-time memo (circle_stats,
#                      2026-08-30). Re-derivable in full — the registers,
#                      the machine commits and close_<OT>.json are the
#                      record; `python coordinator/circle_delta.py --ot <OT>`
#                      regenerates it byte-for-fact.
work/logs/closing_*.json
work/logs/dream_[0-9]*.json
work/logs/delta_[0-9]*.json

# EVERYTHING ELSE A RUN DROPS HERE IS A MEMO — the default is now ignore, and
# the record is re-included by name below. spend_<OT>.json (R380) was the file
# that made the default worth changing: nothing commits it, so every live close
# left one dirty forever, which is the shape that deadlocked a lab `pull-main`.
#
# `work/logs/*` and NOT `work/logs/`, deliberately, exactly as `work/sandbox/*`
# above: git cannot re-include anything beneath an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so the
# directory form would silently defeat all four negations.
#
# THE NEGATIONS ARE LOAD-BEARING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, and this is the one place
# in the file where that is true of a machine path rather than a human one:
#   close_*.json   transcript_store.circle_commit_paths() puts it in EVERY
#                  circle's own commit, live and sandbox. It is new and
#                  untracked at each close, and `git add --` REFUSES the whole
#                  path list when one member is ignored — so ignoring it would
#                  raise GitError out of circle_commit() into /close, which
#                  catches only ImportError. It is also the record
#                  circle_state.py, circle_delta.py and
#                  circle_close_verify.py --reconcile all read.
#   */ .md .txt    the hand-written build logs, the lab testing transcripts and
#                  the bnf_conformance baseline — 28 tracked files that
#                  gitrepo.system_git_ignored_untrack() would `git rm --cached`
#                  at the next --git-setup. ALL FILES ARE TRACKED IN THE LOCAL
#                  (ruled 2026-08-07).
# `git ls-files --cached --ignored --exclude-standard -- work/logs` is the
# check: it must stay EMPTY, because that set is exactly what --git-setup drops.
#
# work/logs/circle_audit*.log stays spelled out above and below: REQUIRED_IGNORES
# in gitrepo.py matches by exact string, so the blanket does not satisfy it and
# --git-setup would re-append the line on every run.
work/logs/*
!work/logs/close_*.json
!work/logs/*/
!work/logs/*.md
!work/logs/*.txt

# THE DIAGNOSTIC NOTES a refused check writes — work/diagnostics/gate_<time>.md,
# 2026-08-26. Each is written FOR its reader, who may hand-edit it before
# sending it anywhere; a copy in the history would be a second version they did
# not choose. The screen names the path, which is where it lives.
work/diagnostics/

# WHICH MEMORY IS THE EXPERIMENT — work/memory_probe_planted.toml,
# 2026-08-28. A planted record stopped carrying its own probe label when R372
# began showing a memory's circle tag to the part, so the identity moved to a
# file instead. It is lab scratch between a `seed` and its `unseed`, it is
# never true of any tree but the one mid-run, and committing it would put the
# answer sheet in the history of the thing being tested.
work/memory_probe_planted.toml

