work/issue_trial/

# Claude Code CLI's own scheduler lock — rewritten by the harness itself,
# not project content
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Temp workspaces — staging, caches, locks, snapshots
work/circle_audit/

# Run logs — derived, one per run
work/logs/circle_audit*.log

# THE PICTURE OF THE ISSUE GRAPH — work/graph/issue_graph.{svg,html},
# R365, 2026-08-27, the operator's ruling ("local only"). ui/issue_draw.py redraws it at
# the end of every LIVE circle whose graph moved, and commit_circle() commits
# only the circle's own paths, so a TRACKED copy would sit permanently dirty
# in the tree — the exact shape closing_<OT>.json and dream_<OT>.json had
# above, which deadlocked a lab `pull-main` on a dirty tree. Nothing reads
# the picture back: it is for a person to open, and it is rebuilt from
# issues/*.toml, which IS tracked, whenever it falls behind.
#
# EVERY HOOK-REDRAWN PICTURE JOINED IT, 2026-08-30, the operator: *"stop
# saving them and do the merges yourself"*. coordinator_graph.* (ten files)
# and prompt_grammar.* (two) were tracked AND regenerated-and-`git add`ed by
# the pre-commit hook, so any commit touching coordinator/, memory/ or ui/
# python rewrote all ten — and two branches editing UNRELATED modules
# conflicted on every one of them. Git then asked which drawing to keep, of
# the person least able to answer; the honest answer is "neither, redraw
# from the merged source", which is what a generator does in one command.
# A file stored for no reader is the only kind that can conflict for no
# reason. The redraw arms went with the tracking (hook v101) — `git add` on
# an ignored path exits 1, so leaving them would have refused every commit
# in every tree at once.
#
# NAMED FILES, not the directory: work/graph/ also holds the four *_draw.py
# generators, test_coordinator_draw.py, the .psd, the two product_lexicon
# documents, and command_flow.* / system_architecture.* — all still tracked.
# Those last two are redrawn BY HAND, have never been staged by a hook, and
# so have never conflicted; they stay until they do.
work/graph/issue_graph.svg
work/graph/issue_graph.html
# Another group's picture, beside the default group's — audit-register.md #6, 2026-09-08.
# The two literal names above stay: the default group's picture is the one a person has
# open and the one every document points at.
work/graph/issue_graph_*.svg
work/graph/issue_graph_*.html
work/graph/coordinator_graph.svg
work/graph/coordinator_graph.html
work/graph/coordinator_graph.toml
work/graph/coordinator_graph_live.svg
work/graph/coordinator_graph_live.html
work/graph/coordinator_graph_live.toml
work/graph/coordinator_graph_simple.svg
work/graph/coordinator_graph_simple.html
work/graph/coordinator_graph_live_simple.svg
work/graph/coordinator_graph_live_simple.html
work/graph/prompt_grammar.svg
work/graph/prompt_grammar.html
work/graph/llm_orchestration.svg
work/graph/llm_orchestration.html

